---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

title: "Release Notes";
description: "Version history and release notes for the Umi‑Time project.";
---

<Base title="Release Notes">
  <div class="umi-region umi-pad">
    <main class="page page-release-notes">
      <header class="page-header">
        <h1>Release Notes</h1>
        <p>
          This page provides version history and release notes for the Umi‑Time
          project. Each release will include details about new features, fixes,
          improvements, and any breaking changes.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Placeholder Release Notes -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>v1.0.0 — Initial Stable Release</h2>
        <h4>November 1, 2026</h4>
        <p>
          The first stable release of Umi‑Time. This version establishes the
          foundation of the Umi‑Time standard and provides a complete,
          production‑ready JavaScript implementation.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            First publication of the <code>umi-time</code> npm package.
          </li>

          <li>
            Introduces the core <code>UmiTime</code> class with an immutable API design
            for predictable, functional behavior.
          </li>

          <li>
            Implements full solar‑geometry support, including:
            <code>solarAltitude</code>, <code>getHourAngle</code>,
            <code>toDeg</code>, <code>toRad</code>, and
            <code>utUmiFromDate</code>.
          </li>

          <li>
            Provides the complete set of Umi‑Time formatting specifications:
            <code>UMI_COMPACT</code>, <code>UMI_COMPACT_BARE</code>,
            <code>UMI_EXTENDED</code>, <code>UMI_EXTENDED_BARE</code>,
            <code>UMI_DATE_TIME</code>, <code>UMI_DATE_TIME_EXT</code>,
            <code>UMI_CANONICAL_FULL</code>, and
            <code>UMI_CANONICAL_FULL_EXT</code>.
          </li>

          <li>
            Ships comprehensive TypeScript definitions via
            <code>dist/index.d.ts</code>.
          </li>

          <li>
            Provides a browser‑ready global bundle:
            <code>dist/umi-time.min.js</code>, exposing <code>UmiTime</code> as a
            global for CDN and script‑tag usage.
          </li>

          <li>
            Launches the documentation site, including examples, demos, and the
            Umi‑Time Manifesto.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Future releases will expand the standard, refine solar calculations,
          introduce additional examples, and continue improving documentation
          and tooling.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Semantic Versioning -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Semantic Versioning</h2>
        <p>
          Umi‑Time follows semantic versioning (<code>MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH</code>).
          Breaking changes will increment the major version, new features will
          appear in minor releases, and fixes or refinements will be included in
          patch releases.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Where Releases Are Published -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Where Releases Are Published</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>npm:</strong> <code>umi-time</code> package</li>
          <li><strong>GitHub:</strong> tagged releases with changelogs</li>
          <li><strong>Website:</strong> this Release Notes page</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Feedback -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Feedback</h2>
        <p>
          If you notice an issue in a release or want to propose improvements,
          please open an issue on GitHub or visit the
          <a href="/contributing">Contributing</a> page.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Base>
